@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.
   The <page-header> tag helper in SyncAudit.cshtml comes from Humans.UI and needs the
   @addTagHelper line, not just the @using; an unbound tag helper survives into the response
   as its own start tag rather than throwing (G5-SECTION-TEMPLATE.md step 12).
   Guarded by MonitorPageRenderTests.

   No @inject IStringLocalizer line: the section carries no resource set at all. Its one page
   is admin-only English (design §3b's first question), and
   MonitorArchitectureTests.SectionTypesTakeNoStringLocalizer pins that, so the day someone
   adds copy the build tells them to carve a resource set first. *@
@using Humans.Base.Extensions
@using Humans.Monitor
@using Humans.Monitor.Models
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Models
@using Humans.Base.ViewComponents
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
@* <vc:audit-log> (Monitor/SyncAudit) is the AuditLog section's own component; without this
   line the element ships as inert literal markup with a green build. *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.AuditLog
